{
  "description": "The one shape the ruling changes with NO signal to the learner, pinned deliberately. `ol-var-not-visible` fires on a READ; a procedure whose only touch of an invisible name is a WRITE creates its own binding instead, silently and correctly (spec/execution-model.md:443-446 rules it undiagnosable — \"that is a genuinely different variable\"). So `setup` writes 100 into its own `:steps`, the top level still holds 10, and the turtle DRAWS 10 rather than 100 with zero diagnostics. Raised by @turtle-engine in the review gate: the core-language half was covered, but nothing pinned the turtle-VISIBLE half, and a changed picture with no diagnostic is exactly what a rendering fixture is for. The fix a learner needs is one word — `global steps = 10` — which the sibling fixtures cover.",
